  "summary": {
    "en": "Egypt reopened its embassy in Tripoli after a 12‑year closure, restoring diplomatic presence in Libya. A UK court upheld a decision against the government in a case involving a Syrian asylum seeker who was kidnapped in Libya. The 22nd meeting of the Sahel-Saharan bloc’s Executive Council was held in Tripoli, bringing regional officials to the capital. Russia and Libya discussed bilateral trade and investment in an October 2026 update. Combat intensity remains low, with 2 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.",
